```

Proposition 3.3 applies at this same radius-two place: `M_2,M_3<=e=98`, the
probe detects `g,f,T_2`, and `ord g<0`.  Consequently

```text
(T_3^psi)_f(sigma)=c_f H(pi)^22 t^-44+...,  c_f!=0.
```

This is the formal `f`-derivative, not `T_3` itself, and it is not moved to a
child place.  The next step uses the prompt's explicit reading of p.209's term
as **radius-two leading data**: all 40 roots represented by the corner follow
this place, and no omitted term has smaller `e-k`.  Moh does not define the
ellipsis well enough on pp.209--210 to prove that support assertion.  Under
that declared premise, `15-40=-25` and one may write

```text
