   216	monomials alone do not exclude C, and one must not silently assume that every
   217	`Omega(P)` is polynomial.
   218	
   219	Finally, the coordinate determinant is
   220	
   221	```text
   222	det D(X,Y)/D(x,y) = det D(x^-1,a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2+x^3y)/D(x,y) = -x.
   223	```
   224	
   225	If the original constant is `J(f,g)=c`, then
   226	`J(Omega f,Omega g)=-c*x`; Moh's displayed `+x` fixes `c=-1` (or uses the
   227	equivalent sign normalization).  The driver checks this orientation and the
   228	positive controls `J(x^2/2,y)=x`, `J(x^5/5,y)=x^4`.
   229	
   230	## 3. Shape from old-coordinate polynomiality
   231	
   232	Let `P(X,Y)=sum_{i+j<=D} p_ij X^iY^j`.  Its literal transform is
   233	
   234	```text
   235	Omega(P)=sum p_ij x^-i(a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2+x^3y)^j.                 (3.1)
   236	```
   237	
   238	Conversely, on a monomial,
   239	
   240	```text
   241	Omega^-1(x^e y^k)
   242	 = X^(k-e) [X^2(Y-a_0)-a_1X-a_2]^k.                            (3.2)
   243	```
   244	
   245	Equations (3.1)--(3.2), not a guessed polygon, are the exact polynomiality
   246	test: negative `X` powers and terms of total degree greater than `D` must cancel
   247	after coefficients with the same image are combined.  A single old monomial
   248	can only produce
   249	
   250	```text
   251	0<=k<=D,             4k-D <= e <= 2D+k,
   252	```
   253	
   254	but membership in this envelope is not sufficient, because inverse-image
   255	coefficients are correlated.
   256	
   257	Combining the top and radius-two weights gives the following useful maximal
   258	Laurent envelopes:
   259	
   260	```text
   261	F:  max(k-12,4k-66)  <= e <= 132+k, 0<=k<=66;
   262	G:  max(k-18,4k-99)  <= e <= 198+k, 0<=k<=99;
   263	T2: max(k-10,4k-55)  <= e <= 110+k, 0<=k<=55;
   264	T3: max(k-25,4k-145) <= e <= 290+k, 0<=k<=145.
   265	```
   266	
   267	They contain `6187,13816,4316,29441` lattice sites.  If one adds the separate,
   268	unproved requirement `Omega(P) in k[x,y]`, intersecting with `e>=0` leaves
   269	`6109,13645,4261,29116` sites.  The branch-C faces displayed above have minimum
   270	`x`-exponents `-6,-9,-5`, but those face minima are not lower bounds for the
   271	full Laurent support: for example, an interior old-coordinate monomial may map
   272	to a more negative pure `x` power without changing either displayed face.
   273	These are `COUNTING-BOUND` support-site counts, never independent-variable
   274	counts.
   275	
   276	A more stringent calculation shows exactly why the printed information does
   277	not yield Moh's 11.  In a straightened two-arc **slice**, define
   278	
   279	```text
   280	K(x,w)=x^11 h(x^-1,w/x)=sum_i x^i P_i(w),  deg P_i<=11-i.
   281	```
   282	
   283	The minor order `ord h=-2` requires `i+3j>=9` at `w=0`; the major order
   284	`ord h=-1/3` requires `3i+4j>=32` at `w=1`.  Hence
   285	
   286	```text
   287	w^3(w-1)^8,
   288	x^3 w^2(w-1)^6, x^4 w^2(w-1)^5,
   289	x^6 w(w-1)^4, x^7 w(w-1)^3, x^8 w(w-1)^2,
   290	x^9(w-1)^2, x^10(w-1), x^11                              (3.3)
   291	```
   292	
   293	is a basis: dimension 9, or eight free coefficients after monicity.  The
   294	minor initial cubic is
   295	`pi^3+c_3 pi^2+c_6 pi+c_9`.  Translating its double root to zero gives
   296	`c_6=c_9=0`; requiring `Omega(h)` polynomial then gives `c_10=0`.  Five
   297	coefficients remain, with `c_3!=0` distinguishing B from the triple-root
   298	degeneration, and
   299	
   300	```text
   301	Omega(h)=x*y^3(x^4y-1)^8
   302	 +c_3*y^2(x^4y-1)^6+c_4*x*y^2(x^4y-1)^5
   303	 +c_7*y(x^4y-1)^3+c_8*x*y(x^4y-1)^2+c_11.                  (3.4)
   304	```
   305	
   306	`TYPE[GAUGE-SLICE]`: (3.3)--(3.4) are rigorous after straightening the two
   307	arcs, but p.209 retains `a_0,a_1,a_2` and does not prove that the straightening
   308	preserves both filtrations and old-coordinate polynomiality.  Thus (3.4) is
   309	not promoted as Moh's literal ansatz.
