   444	
   445	```text
   446	[z^j] rem_z(4f_2-U^2, D)=0,       j=0,1,2,3,4,         (5.12)
   447	D=z^3(z+3a)^2.
   448	```
   449	
   450	Equation (5.12) is an exact finite system, not a degree heuristic.  Its first
   451	three displayed rows are
   452	
   453	```text
   454	4*f2_0-v0^2,
   455	4*f2_1-2*v0*v1,
   456	4*f2_2-2*v0*v2-v1^2,
   457	```
   458	
   459	where `U=sum_(i=0)^7 v_i z^i`; the last two expanded rows and their declared
   460	generator order are in `local_band_audit.json`.  Equivalently, without hiding
   461	any branch,
   462	
   463	```text
   464	f_2=(U^2+D*(w0+w1*z+...+w10*z^10))/4.                 (5.13)
   465	```
   466	
   467	Under (5.13), the rational block in (5.11) becomes polynomial because
   468	`D^2/H^3=z+3a`.  A separate abstract-jet substitution checks (5.10) exactly.
   469	It also checks that `q_4-q4_tail` has degree at most 22, so
   470	
   471	```text
   472	g_4^new=(3H^3 f_4^new-(q_4-q4_tail))/2
   473	```
   474	
   475	lies in the allowed window.  The operator has 22 `Q*` pivots, one `H^7`
   476	resonance, and 14 common `f_4` directions.  The five equations (5.12) are
   477	independent in the triangular parameterization.  Hence band 4 is consistent
   478	with cumulative fibre dimension 50, or 51 including `a`.  This is the deepest
   479	fully certified consistent band in this report.
   480	
   481	### Exact next system: band 5
   482	
   483	The band-2 generators now supply fixed tails.  With the same notation as
   484	(5.9),
   485	
   486	```text
   487	tail_f5=-sum_(k=0)^15 v1F2(k)*[z^k]f_2*z^(k+1),
   488	tail_g5=-sum_(k=0)^24 v1G2(k)*[z^k]g_2*z^(k+1),
   489	q5_tail=3H^3 tail_f5-2tail_g5,                          (5.14)
   490	```
   491	
   492	where
   493	
   494	```text
   495	v1F2=(7,9,11,13,16,18,20,22,25,27,29,31,34,36,38,40),
   496	v1G2=(10,13,15,17,19,22,24,26,28,31,33,35,37,40,42,44,
   497	      46,49,51,53,55,58,60,62,64).
   498	```
   499	
   500	Let `deg f_5^new<=12`, `deg g_5^new<=21`.  The 35 new unknowns occur in
   501	
   502	```text
   503	E_5=sum_(r+s=5)((18-s)f_r'g_s+(r-12)f_rg_s')=0.        (5.15)
   504	```
   505	
   506	An exact particular normal form is
   507	
   508	```text
   509	q_5=-(3/2)(f_1f_4+f_2f_3)/H^3
   510	    +(3/8)(f_1^2f_3+f_1f_2^2)/H^9-(3/16)f_1^3f_2/H^15
   511	    +(3/128)f_1^5/H^21+(4/3)b_2H^2f_3
   512	    +(4/9)b_2f_1f_2/H^4-(4/81)b_2f_1^3/H^10
   513	    +(7/6)b_4Hf_1.                                     (5.16)
   514	```
   515	
   516	Write `s=z+3a`, `f_2=(U^2+z^3s^2V)/4`, with `deg U<=7` and `deg V<=10`.
   517	The exact old-parameter compatibility system is the eight rows
   518	
   519	```text
   520	[z^j] rem_z(N_5,M_5)=0,             j=0,...,7,         (5.17)
   521	M_5=z^6s^2,
   522	N_5=243UV^2-3888z^3sVf_3+640b_2z^4sU^3.
   523	```
   524	
   525	The full expanded rows, generator order, and zero handling are in
   526	`local_band_audit.json`.  For orientation the first three are
   527	
   528	```text
   529	243*v0*w0^2,
   530	486*v0*w0*w1+243*v1*w0^2,
   531	486*v0*w0*w2+243*v0*w1^2+486*v1*w0*w1+243*v2*w0^2.
   532	```
   533	
   534	If (5.17) holds, the apparent degrees 22 through 25 of
   535	`q_5-q5_tail` cancel identically.  The remaining operator has rank 22 and a
   536	13-dimensional new kernel before the eight nonlinear old-parameter
   537	conditions.  Those eight rows have not been decomposed or solved, so no
   538	post-band-5 dimension and no consistency claim is made.
   539	
   540	To continue beyond (5.17), one must also restore the curved `u` chart and the
   541	canonical `T_2,T_3` coefficient relations.  Continuing only the zero-jet
   542	slice cannot decide the full branch even if it later becomes empty.
   543	
   544	## 6. Xu's `delta=5/2` split
   545	
   546	Xu's leading data at `delta=5/2` are
   547	
   548	```text
   549	f(sigma)       = p(pi)^6  t^-3   + ...,
   550	g(sigma)       = p(pi)^9  t^-9/2 + ...,
   551	T2(sigma)      = p(pi)^5  t^-5/2 + ...,
   552	(T3)_f(sigma)  = p(pi)^22 t^-11  + ...,
   553	T3(sigma)      = q(pi)    t^-5   + ...,
   554	deg p=3,       deg q=40.
   555	```
   556	
   557	Put `x=s^2`, `y=pi/s`.  Then
   558	
   559	```text
   560	Omega(P)(s^2,pi/s)
   561	 =P(s^-2,a_0+a_1s^2+a_2s^4+pi*s^5).
   562	```
   563	
   564	Integer `x` exponents force `p^6` to be even in `s`.  For monic
   565	`p=z^3+A z^2+Bz+C`, the nine odd coefficient rows have triangular leading
   566	pivots
   567	
   568	```text
   569	[z^17]p^6=6A,
   570	[z^15]p^6 |_(A=0)=6C.

