+system.
+
+To continue beyond (5.17), one must also restore the curved `u` chart and the
+canonical `T_2,T_3` coefficient relations.  Continuing only the zero-jet
+slice cannot decide the full branch even if it later becomes empty.
+
+## 6. Xu's `delta=5/2` split
+
+Xu's leading data at `delta=5/2` are
+
+```text
+f(sigma)       = p(pi)^6  t^-3   + ...,
+g(sigma)       = p(pi)^9  t^-9/2 + ...,
+T2(sigma)      = p(pi)^5  t^-5/2 + ...,
+(T3)_f(sigma)  = p(pi)^22 t^-11  + ...,
+T3(sigma)      = q(pi)    t^-5   + ...,
+deg p=3,       deg q=40.
+```
+
+Put `x=s^2`, `y=pi/s`.  Then
+
+```text
+Omega(P)(s^2,pi/s)
+ =P(s^-2,a_0+a_1s^2+a_2s^4+pi*s^5).
+```
+
+Integer `x` exponents force `p^6` to be even in `s`.  For monic
+`p=z^3+A z^2+Bz+C`, the nine odd coefficient rows have triangular leading
+pivots
+
+```text
+[z^17]p^6=6A,
+[z^15]p^6 |_(A=0)=6C.
+```
+
+Hence
+
+```text
+p=z(z^2-rho),        rho != 0,        disc(p)=4rho^3.  (6.1)
+```
+
+The parity saturation is explicit.  In `Q[U,A,C,B]` with lex order, add
+`UB-1`.  The wrapped reduced basis is `{UB-1,A,C}`; the wrapper-only and raw
+parity ideals are nonunit, while adjoining `B` gives `[1]`.  The point
+`A=C=0,B=-1,U=-1` is a positive control.  Then set `B=-rho`.
+
+This separates the levels correctly: at radius two the strict-below common
+face is still `z^3`; at radius `5/2` the at-level polynomial is (6.1).  The
+three roots describe a `9+9+9` split of cover roots.  The two roots
+`+sqrt(rho)` and `-sqrt(rho)` are exchanged by denominator-two conjugacy and
+are not thereby proved to be two physical places.
+
+Xu's factorization `q=p^10 q_1`, `deg q_1=10`, reduces
+`p q'-10p'q=kappa*p^14` exactly to
+
+```text
+q_1'=kappa*p^3.
+```
+
+In the monic `T_3` gauge `kappa=10`, and direct integration gives
+
+```text
+q_1=z^10-(15/4)rho*z^8+5rho^2*z^6-(5/2)rho^3*z^4+b_0. (6.2)
+```
+
+Xu's displayed `kappa=-2` is a scalar-equivalent normalization.  In the exact
+ring
+
+```text
+Q[T,b1,...,b9,kappa,b0,rho], lex,  T*rho*kappa-1=0,
+```
+
+there are 12 unknowns excluding the wrapper and ten effective coefficient
+rows.  The reduced component is
+
+```text
+b1,b2,b3, 2b4+5rho^3, b5, b6-5rho^2, b7,
+4b8+15rho, b9, kappa-10.
+```
+
+It has dimension two, with parameters `(rho,b_0)`.  The wrapped ideal is
+nonunit; adjoining `rho` or `kappa` gives `[1]`, and
+`rho=b_0=1,kappa=10,T=1/10` is a positive witness.
+Moreover,
+
+```text
+Res_z(p,q_1)=b_0(4b_0-rho^5)^2/16.
+```
+
+Thus the same witness lies on the optional coprime open; coprimality is not
+needed merely for face survival.
+
+For `u=xy^2`, define
+
+```text
+Hhat=y(u-rho),
+F*=Hhat^6, G*=Hhat^9, T2*=Hhat^5,
+R*=Hhat^10*(u^5-(15/4)rho*u^4+5rho^2*u^3
+             -(5/2)rho^3*u^2+b_0).
+```
+
+Direct differentiation gives
+
+```text
+J(F*,G*)=0,                 J(R*,G*)=45*x*Hhat^22.
+```
+
+All faces pass the inverse-`Omega` old-degree test termwise; maximum degrees
+are `11,66,99,55,145` for `Hhat,F*,G*,T2*,R*`.  The verdict is exactly
+
+```text
+SURVIVES[DELTA-5/2-LEADING-FACE].
+```
+
+It is not a full lift and does not contradict the fixed-radius branch-C
+exclusion.
+
+## 7. Controls
+
+### 7.1 Branch A predecessor
+
+The charged predecessor uses
+
+```text
+h=y^8(y-x)+sum_(j=0)^8 h_0_j y^j,
+A=(h-h|_(y=0))/y,
+beta=bp*A+bq*y+br*x+bs,
+alpha=quotient_y(beta^2,h),
+f=h^2+2beta,
+g=h^3+3beta*h+(3/2)alpha.
+```
+
+In `Q[h_0_8,...,h_0_0,bp,bq,br,bs,c,T]`, the 29 `h`-adic/Jacobian rows have
+14 unknowns excluding `T`.  The first generator is `-c`; after adding
+`Tc-1`,
+
+```text
+1=-(Tc-1)-T(-c).                                         (7.1)
+```
+
+The unsaturated ideal is nonunit.  Exact `Q` and primes
+`32003,32009,32027` all return `[1]`, with declared-ring and wrapper controls.
+This replays `[1]` for `SATURATED-EMPTY[CONTROL-ANSATZ]`; it does not construct
+the missing bridge to Moh's unprinted ten-variable branch-A system.
+
+### 7.2 Branch C
+
+For squarefree `H=z(z-a)(z-b)` with `ab(a-b)k != 0`, the fixed-radius ODE
+forces `R=H^13(z+ell)` and then
+
+```text
+H'(z+ell)+2H-kH=0.
+```
+
+Writing its four coefficient rows as
+
+```text
+f1=5-k,
+f2=(k-4)(a+b)+3ell,
+f3=(3-k)ab-2(a+b)ell,
+f4=ab*ell,
+f5=T*ab(a-b)k-1,
+```
+
+put `s=a+b,p=ab,d=a-b` and
+
+```text
+m1=Tdk(p/2-ell*s), m2=-Tdk*ell, m3=-Tdk/2,
+m4=3T^2d^2k^2ell, m5=-3Tdk*ell^2-1.
+```
+
+Direct expansion verifies
+
+```text
+1=m1f1+m2f2+m3f3+m4f4+m5f5.                            (7.2)
+```
+
+The unsaturated system has a witness (`a=b=ell=0,k=5`), while the wrapped
+system is `[1]` over `Q` and the same three primes.  Thus branch C is
+`SATURATED-EMPTY[FIXED-RADIUS-TWO]`, with no claim about a different radius.
+
+### 7.3 Moh `(16,12)` Appendix-II calibration
+
+Moh p.208 prints the source-shaped `h,A,B,alpha_i,beta_i` ansatz.  Its 77
+Jacobian coefficient equations have 18 unknowns including `c` (plus wrapper
+`T`); the exact rational wrapped ideal is `[1]`, while the raw origin control
+is nonunit.
+
+The independent order-spine replay begins with 23 rows in 18 chart unknowns.
+By descending `h` band it has row counts
+
+```text
+h^5:1, h^4:2, h^3:2, h^2:5, h^1:6, h^0:7.
+```
+
+Seven `Q*` pivots, with coefficients
+
+```text
+3,6,3,6,3,-12,-9/4,
+```
+
+leave 15 rows in 11 unknowns.  The resolved ring map was checked on all 23
+original generators.  The remaining positive grading permits the torus slice
+`x=1`; over `Q[y]/(H)` with
+
+```text
+H=54y^2-36y+5,
+```
+
+four affine pivots leave the coefficient-field unit
+
+```text
+u=20y-10/3,       v=27/10-27y/5,
+u*v-1=-2H,        hence 1=u*v+2H.                       (7.3)
+```
+
+This is the required positive calibration:
+`SATURATED-EMPTY[ORDER-CHART-CONTROL]`.  It demonstrates that the lifting
+machinery can terminate at the known Appendix-II contradiction without
+pretending the replay variables are Moh's unprinted eta variables.
+
