@@ -0,0 +1,845 @@
+# Moh `(99,66)`, branch B: a banded lift and the `delta=5/2` face
+
+## Verdict first
+
+The requested full branch-B coefficient variety is **not decided** by the
+frozen sources or by the bounded computation below.  Its typed lane verdict is
+
+```text
+COUNTING-BOUND[B-FULL-LIFT]
+```
+
+This is a substantive stop, not a renaming of face survival.  The conditional
+radius-two face is nonempty, and an old-polynomial, two-face, zero-jet slice of
+the Jacobian equations is consistent through band 5 and completely counted
+through band 4.  The fifth-band system is printed exactly below.  However,
+Moh's pp.209--210 do not
+print the filtration-preserving change that produces his 11 variables, and an
+independent curved-centre calculation finds a surviving symbolic jet
+`u=a_1`.  Therefore setting `a_1=0` has not been proved to preserve either the
+full coefficient variety or emptiness.  The slice cannot certify a full lift.
+
+The scoped results are:
+
+| object | typed result | what was actually checked |
+|---|---|---|
+| branch-B radius-two leader | `SURVIVES[PRINTED-LEADER-ODE-FACE]` | exact localized ideal, conditional on `T_3` being the radius-two leader |
+| branch-B band lift | `COUNTING-BOUND[ZERO-JET-TWO-FACE-SLICE]` | consistent through band 5; exact dimension 51 including `a` after band 4 at fixed `c` |
+| full Moh `(99,66)` branch B | `COUNTING-BOUND[B-FULL-LIFT]` | no source-licensed map from the curved chart to Moh's unprinted 11 variables |
+| Xu `delta=5/2` split | `SURVIVES[DELTA-5/2-LEADING-FACE]` | exact face ideal, dimension 2 (`rho,b_0`) |
+| branch-A predecessor control | `SATURATED-EMPTY[CONTROL-ANSATZ]` | charged 14-unknown predecessor, not the unprinted ten-variable bridge |
+| branch C at radius two | `SATURATED-EMPTY[FIXED-RADIUS-TWO]` | exact rational certificate and three finite-field replays |
+| Moh `(16,12)` control | `SATURATED-EMPTY[ORDER-CHART-CONTROL]` | source-shaped system and second-spine terminal unit |
+
+No polynomial pair of degrees `(99,66)` is produced, so there is no
+`REPRESENTATIVE` to print and no Keller/counterexample claim.  In particular,
+the identities involving `F_2,G_2,T_{3,2}` below are identities of leading
+faces, not `J(F,G)=constant` for a completed old-coordinate pair.  There is no
+new exit price or first-separation assertion, hence no `charge_basis` line.
+
+## 1. Custody, source boundary, and reproducibility
+
+Before reading the mathematics, the lane receipt
+`xmodel/moh9966-B-lift-sol56-20260903.run.v2` was parsed mechanically.  The
+manifest was generated from its indexed `charged_input_*_basename` and
+`charged_input_*_sha256` fields and piped to `sha256sum -c`; all 12 frozen files
+under `/tmp/jc2-lane.kNGcqH/inputs` returned `OK`.  No digest from the prompt was
+retyped.  The command was:
+
+```bash
+awk -F= -v d='/tmp/jc2-lane.kNGcqH/inputs/' \
+  '/^charged_input_[0-9]+_basename=/{split($1,a,"_"); b[a[3]]=$2} \
+   /^charged_input_[0-9]+_sha256=/{split($1,a,"_"); h[a[3]]=$2} \
+   END{for(i=1;i<=12;i++) print h[i] "  " d b[i]}' \
+  xmodel/moh9966-B-lift-sol56-20260903.run.v2 | sha256sum -c
+```
+
+The frozen Moh PDF was read at printed pp.149, 194--195, 202, and 207--210.
+The source boundary matters.  Page 209 prints the transform and the four
+leading corners.  Page 210 says that simultaneous work in
+`k<<x^-1>>` and `k<<y^-1>>` reduces the problem to 11 variables, but it gives
+neither those variables, their support, the gauge map, nor the resulting
+equations.  The following pages treat another row.  Thus the number 11 is not
+an executable coefficient system.
+
+The frozen Xu PDF was read at printed/PDF p.12, equation (7.1), and p.13,
+section 8.  Xu supplies the `delta=5/2` leading expansion and calls the
+`(99,66)` case open.  Prime marks used for tower labels are not interpreted as
+derivatives; derivatives below are written `d/dz`.
+
+Generated artifacts are confined to `box/moh9966lift-20260903/`.  No ledger,
+`jc2-lean`, prohibited `ideation-*` file, or named live-lane report was edited.
+
+## 2. Coordinates and exact old-polynomiality
+
+Use capitals `(X,Y)` for the original polynomial coordinates and lower-case
+`(x,y)` after Moh's transform:
+
+```text
+X = x^-1,
+Y = a_0 + a_1*x + a_2*x^2 + x^3*y,
+z = x*y + a_2.
+```
+
+For a transformed monomial the inverse is exact:
+
+```text
+Omega^-1(x^e y^j)
+ = X^(j-e) [X^2(Y-a_0)-a_1 X-a_2]^j.                 (2.1)
+```
+
+Consequently old polynomiality is not the condition that each displayed
+Laurent monomial separately has nonnegative `x` exponent.  One must combine
+equal inverse images, require the complete negative-`X` tail to vanish, and
+impose total degrees 66, 99, 55, and 145 on `F,G,T_2,T_3`.  For an individual
+monomial, the convenient sufficient test is
+
+```text
+j-e >= 0,                 4j-e <= D.                  (2.2)
+```
+
+All four faces printed in section 4 pass (2.2) term by term.  Full tails would
+still have to be tested after combination by (2.1).
+
+For the finite coefficient spaces, put `w=xY` and, for an old polynomial `P`
+of degree at most `D`,
+
+```text
+K_D(x,w)=x^D P(x^-1,w/x)=sum_r x^r P_r(w),
+0 <= r,                  deg_w P_r <= D-r.            (2.3)
+```
+
+In the straightened zero-jet slice (`a_0=a_1=a_2=0`) the radius-two centre is
+`w=x^3z`.  If the local pole magnitude is `L`, its order condition is
+
+```text
+r + 3 ord_w(P_r) >= D-L.                               (2.4)
+```
+
+At the major direction `w=1`, radius `1/3` is integralized as
+
+```text
+3r + 4 ord_(w-1)(P_r) >= 3(D+m),                       (2.5)
+```
+
+where `m` is the major order of `P`.  Equality supplies the fixed face;
+adding one to both right sides gives the strict perturbation space.
+
+Moh's Theorem 1.2 gives the same filtration in approximate-root notation.  If
+`P=h^d+sum_i alpha_i h^(d-i)` and `ord h(sigma)=lambda/d`, then
+
+```text
+ord alpha_i(sigma) >= i*(lambda/d).                    (2.6)
+```
+
+At the radius-two probe used here, `ord h=-2`, so (2.6) reads
+`ord alpha_i >= -2i` (and likewise for the `beta_i`).  If `delta*=2` denotes
+the positive pole magnitude, this is `-i delta*`; this sign convention must
+not be silently reversed.  At the major `1/3` face it reads `>=-i/3`.
+The further major radius `4/9` is recorded by the tower, but its scalar value
+does not specify the missing centre/evaluation functional in pp.209--210.
+It therefore cannot safely be turned into additional coefficient rows by
+analogy.
+
+For (2.4)--(2.5), define
+
+```text
+v0=max(0,ceil((D-L+1-r)/3)),
+v1=max(0,ceil((3(D+m)+1-3r)/4)).
+```
+
+After absorbing the scalar `(-1)^v1` into its coefficient, an exact
+strict-face basis element is
+
+```text
+x^L Omega_0(X^(D-r-k-v1) Y^k (Y-X)^v1)
+       = x^n z^k(1-x^3 z)^v1,
+n=r+3k-(D-L),            k=v0,...,D-r-v1.              (2.7)
+```
+
+Thus the Laurent tail at later bands is fixed by the binomial in (2.7); it is
+not a new coefficient.  The mechanically enumerated spaces are:
+
+| object | `(D,L,m)` | non-strict dimension | strict fixed-face kernel |
+|---|---|---:|---:|
+| `F` | `(66,12,-2)` | 181 | 146 |
+| `G` | `(99,18,-3)` | 388 | 336 |
+| `T_2` | `(55,10,-5/3)` | 129 | 100 |
+| `T_3` | `(145,25,-5)` | 816 | 740 |
+
+These are exact old-polynomial counts for the two declared inequalities in
+the stated slice, not the full source filtration and not Moh's 11.  The `F`
+strict generators start in bands 1 through 15 with counts
+
+```text
+17,16,15,14,13,12,11,10,9,8,7,6,4,3,1,
+```
+
+and the `G` generators start in bands 1 through 23 with counts
+
+```text
+26,25,24,23,22,21,20,19,18,17,16,15,14,13,12,11,
+10,9,7,6,4,3,1.
+```
+
+This is a bounded necessary slice in place of a blind 7,326-row expansion.
+
+## 3. Why the zero-jet slice is not the full chart
+
+It is harmless to remove `a_0` by an old polynomial translation, and `a_2`
+can be absorbed into `z` while centring the double root.  The `a_1` term is
+different.  Write `u=a_1`.  For the cubic approximate root,
+
+```text
+K=x^11 h(x^-1,w/x),
+K|_(x=0)=w^3(w-1)^8,
+w=u*x^2+x^3*z.                                         (3.1)
+```
+
+The fixed major face has boundary weight 32, so its strict perturbations obey
+`3r+4q>=33` at `w=1`.  Parameterizing this divisibility first leaves 21
+coefficients.  Expanding (3.1), killing every term below
+`x^9`, and fixing the `x^9` coefficient to
+
+```text
+H=z^2(z+3a)
+```
+
+gives 18 linear equations.  The exact constant-pivot elimination has 18
+`Q*` pivots and no residual equation.  Three tail coefficients remain free:
+
+```text
+c_7_4, c_10_1, c_11_0.
+```
+
+Together with `(a,u)` this is a five-dimensional `h` order space.  Every
+original row was checked after the resolved triangular substitution, and no
+division by `a` or `u` occurred.  In particular, `u` survives symbolically;
+these order rows do not license setting `u=0`.  Later `T_2,T_3` or Jacobian
+rows could still force it.
+
+This calculation is only `H-ORDER-SPACE`, not the full lift: it does not
+invent the unprinted simultaneous Laurent-field gauge, the `4/9` centre, or
+the complete canonical definitions of `T_2^psi,T_3^psi`.  It is nevertheless
+a decisive scope check: no source row yet identifies the zero-jet slice with
+Moh's full coefficient variety, so its nonemptiness or emptiness cannot be
+promoted.
+
+## 4. Radius-two branch-B face
+
+This section is conditional on the banked premise that p.209's printed
+`x^15y^40+...` is the radius-two `T_3` leader.  Moh's ellipsis alone does not
+prove that identification; Xu's further expansion supplies the same datum.
+
+Translate the double root to zero and retain `a != 0`:
+
+```text
+H=z^2(z+3a),
+R=H^12 q,          q=z^4+q3*z^3+q2*z^2+q1*z+q0.
+```
+
+The necessary leader equation is
+
+```text
+2 H R_z - 25 H_z R = k H^14,
+```
+
+or, after division by `H^12`,
+
+```text
+2 H q_z - H_z q - k H^2 = 0.                           (4.1)
+```
+
+The declared ring is
+
+```text
+Q[T,q0,q1,q2,q3,k,a], lex,  T*a*k-1=0.                 (4.2)
+```
+
+There are six unknowns excluding the wrapper and six raw nonzero coefficient
+rows; the last is `2a` times the preceding row, hence five independent rows.
+The exact reduced basis of (4.1)--(4.2) is
+
+```text
+5*T*a-1,
+q0,
+18*a^3+q1,
+3*a^2+q2,
+-4*a+q3,
+k-5.
+```
+
+It is nonunit and one-dimensional.  The wrapper-only and unsaturated ideals
+are also nonunit; adjoining `a` or adjoining `k` makes the wrapped ideal the
+unit ideal.  Therefore
+
+```text
+q=z(z-2a)(z+3a)^2,
+R=z^25(z+3a)^14(z-2a).                                  (4.3)
+```
+
+With `z=xy`, the bivariate faces are
+
+```text
+F_2  = y^12(xy+3a)^6,
+G_2  = y^18(xy+3a)^9,
+T2_2 = y^10(xy+3a)^5,
+T3_2 = y^25(xy+3a)^14(xy-2a).
+```
+
+Direct symbolic differentiation, rather than an ODE inference, gives
+
+```text
+J(F_2,G_2)=0,
+J(T3_2,G_2)=45*x*y^44*(xy+3a)^22.                       (4.4)
+```
+
+The maximum original-coordinate degrees from the termwise inverse test (2.2)
+are respectively `66,99,55,145`.  Equations (4.3)--(4.4) certify
+`SURVIVES[PRINTED-LEADER-ODE-FACE]` only, under that premise.
+
+## 5. Jacobian lift by descending bands
+
+This section works in the explicitly typed slice
+
+```text
+SLICE[Omega_0: X=x^-1, Y=x^3 y; z=xy; fixed top and radius-two faces].
+```
+
+Normalize
+
+```text
+Omega_0(F)=x^-12 f(x,z),       f=sum_(n>=0) x^n f_n(z),
+Omega_0(G)=x^-18 g(x,z),       g=sum_(n>=0) x^n g_n(z),
+f_0=H^6,                       g_0=H^9.
+```
+
+Because `J_(x,y)=x J_(x,z)`, the full transformed Jacobian equation is exactly
+
+```text
+18 f_z g - 12 f g_z + x(f_x g_z-f_z g_x) = c*x^31.     (5.1)
+```
+
+At band `n`, let
+
+```text
+E_n=sum_(r+s=n) ((18-s) f_r' g_s + (r-12) f_r g_s')
+        - c*[n=31].                                    (5.2)
+```
+
+Here a prime in (5.2) means `d/dz`.  With
+
+```text
+q_n=3H^3 f_n-2g_n,
+L_n(q)=2H q' + (n-18)H' q,
+```
+
+the new-variable part is the checked factorization
+
+```text
+E_n(new)=3H^5 L_n(q_n).                                (5.3)
+```
+
+This exposes constant pivots before any nonlinear elimination.  Dimension
+convention: fix one arbitrary nonzero target value of `c` and do not count it;
+the table adds `a` to the coefficient fibre.  The truncated ambient ideal with
+`c` left variable has every listed total increased by one.  The band ledger is:
+
+| band | new unknowns `F+G` | raw / quotient rows | new rank | old compatibility rows | dimension incl. `a`, fixed `c` | result |
+|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
+| 0 | 0 | 0 / 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | face fixed |
+| 1 | `17+26=43` | 32 / 27 | 26 | 0 | 18 | consistent |
+| 2 | `16+25=41` | 36, then 30 / 25 | 24 | 5 | 30 | consistent |
+| 3 | `15+24=39` | 30 / 25 | 24 | 4 | 41 | consistent |
+| 4 | `14+23=37` | 29 / 24 | 22 | 5 | 51 | consistent |
+| 5 | `13+22=35` | 28 / 23 after compatibility | 22 | 8 nonlinear | `>=59` | consistent subfamily; full dimension open |
+
+Dimensions are fibre parameter counts with the target scalar `c` held fixed;
+the last column adds the localized face parameter `a`.  If `c` is retained as
+an unknown in these early truncations, add one.  The scalar does not enter an
+equation until band 31, so early consistency says nothing about realizing
+`c != 0`.
+
+### Band 1
+
+Take `deg f_1<=16`, `deg g_1<=25`.  The 32 nonzero coefficients of `E_1`
+range from `z^11` through `z^42`.  Dividing the known factor `3H^5` leaves 27
+nonzero coefficient rows.  The operator has rank 26; the 26 `g_1`
+coefficients are `Q*` pivots of coefficient `-2`.  There is one dependent
+coefficient row but no polynomial kernel: `L_1(q)=0` would require
+`q` proportional to `H^(17/2)`.  Thus the solution in the degree window is
+
+```text
+g_1=(3/2)H^3 f_1.                                      (5.4)
+```
+
+Thus 17 fibre parameters remain.
+
+### Band 2
+
+There are 41 new coefficients.  Polynomial solvability of (5.3) imposes five
+conditions on the old band:
+
+```text
+H^3 | f_1^2.
+```
+
+On `a != 0`, this is equivalently
+
+```text
+D | f_1,       D=z^3(z+3a)^2,
+f_1=D U,       deg U<=11.                               (5.5)
+```
+
+The new operator rank is 24, leaving a 17-dimensional new kernel.  An exact
+normal form is
+
+```text
+q_2=-(3/4)f_1^2/H^3 + b_2 H^8.                         (5.6)
+```
+
+The five old conditions reduce the preceding 17 parameters to 12, hence the
+cumulative fibre dimension is `12+17=29`, or 30 including `a`.
+
+### Band 3
+
+The 39 new coefficients have rank 24.  Four additional old-parameter rows
+upgrade (5.5) to
+
+```text
+H^3 | f_1,
+f_1=H^3 U,       deg U<=7,                              (5.7)
+q_3=-(3/2)U f_2 +(1/8)U^3 +(4/3)b_2 H^5 U.             (5.8)
+```
+
+The exact differential-polynomial identity obtained by substituting
+(5.4), (5.6), and (5.8) into (5.2) was checked before coefficient expansion.
+After the four old conditions, the cumulative fibre dimension is 40, or 41
+including `a`.
+
+The fixed old-polynomial base contributes at this band:
+
+```text
+W_3=-8z^4-18a z^3,
+f_3=6H^5W_3+sum_(i=0)^14 f3_i z^i,
+g_3=9H^8W_3+g_3^new.                                  (5.8a)
+```
+
+Every later occurrence of `f_3` means this total polynomial, not only its 15
+new coefficients.
+
+### Band 4
+
+Band 4 is not a fresh 37-coefficient polynomial ansatz: band-1 basis elements
+from (2.7) contribute fixed binomial tails.  If `v1F(k)` and `v1G(k)` denote
+their `(Y-X)` exponents, then
+
+```text
+tail_f4=-sum_(k=0)^16 v1F(k)*[z^k]f_1*z^(k+1),
+tail_g4=-sum_(k=0)^25 v1G(k)*[z^k]g_1*z^(k+1),
+q4_tail=3H^3 tail_f4-2tail_g4,                          (5.9)
+```
+
+with the exact arrays
+
+```text
+v1F=(7,10,12,14,16,19,21,23,25,28,30,32,34,37,39,41,43),
+v1G=(11,13,16,18,20,22,25,27,29,31,34,36,38,40,43,45,
+     47,49,52,54,56,58,61,63,65,67).
+```
+
+Let `f_4^new` and `g_4^new` have degrees at most 13 and 22.  The exact
+coefficient equation is
+
+```text
+E_4=sum_(r+s=4)((18-s)f_r'g_s+(r-12)f_rg_s')=0,        (5.10)
+```
+
+where `f_4=tail_f4+f_4^new` and similarly for `g_4`.  Its rational normal form
+is represented by
+
+```text
+q_4= -(3/2)f_1 f_3/H^3 -(3/4)f_2^2/H^3
+     +(3/8)f_1^2 f_2/H^9 -(3/64)f_1^4/H^15
+     +(4/3)b_2 H^2 f_2 +(2/9)b_2 f_1^2/H^4+b_4H^7.    (5.11)
+```
+
+After (5.7), polynomiality and the degree/tail window reduce to the five exact
+remainder equations
+
+```text
+[z^j] rem_z(4f_2-U^2, D)=0,       j=0,1,2,3,4,         (5.12)
+D=z^3(z+3a)^2.
+```
+
+Equation (5.12) is an exact finite system, not a degree heuristic.  Its first
+three displayed rows are
+
+```text
+4*f2_0-v0^2,
+4*f2_1-2*v0*v1,
+4*f2_2-2*v0*v2-v1^2,
+```
+
+where `U=sum_(i=0)^7 v_i z^i`; the last two expanded rows are in
+`local_band_audit.json`.  Equivalently, without hiding any branch,
+
+```text
+f_2=(U^2+D*(w0+w1*z+...+w10*z^10))/4.                 (5.13)
+```
+
+Under (5.13), the rational block in (5.11) becomes polynomial because
+`D^2/H^3=z+3a`.  A separate abstract-jet substitution checks (5.10) exactly.
+It also checks that `q_4-q4_tail` has degree at most 22, so
+
+```text
+g_4^new=(3H^3 f_4^new-(q_4-q4_tail))/2
+```
+
+lies in the allowed window.  The operator has 22 `Q*` pivots, one `H^7`
+resonance, and 14 common `f_4` directions.  The five equations (5.12) are
+independent in the triangular parameterization.  Hence band 4 is consistent
+with cumulative fibre dimension 50, or 51 including `a`.  This is the deepest
+band with a complete dimension count in this report.
+
+### Exact next system: band 5
+
+The band-2 generators now supply fixed tails.  With the same notation as
+(5.9),
+
+```text
+tail_f5=-sum_(k=0)^15 v1F2(k)*[z^k]f_2*z^(k+1),
+tail_g5=-sum_(k=0)^24 v1G2(k)*[z^k]g_2*z^(k+1),
+q5_tail=3H^3 tail_f5-2tail_g5,                          (5.14)
+```
+
+where
+
+```text
+v1F2=(7,9,11,13,16,18,20,22,25,27,29,31,34,36,38,40),
+v1G2=(10,13,15,17,19,22,24,26,28,31,33,35,37,40,42,44,
+      46,49,51,53,55,58,60,62,64).
+```
+
+Let `deg f_5^new<=12`, `deg g_5^new<=21`.  The 35 new unknowns occur in
+
+```text
+E_5=sum_(r+s=5)((18-s)f_r'g_s+(r-12)f_rg_s')=0.        (5.15)
+```
+
+An exact particular normal form is
+
+```text
+q_5=-(3/2)(f_1f_4+f_2f_3)/H^3
+    +(3/8)(f_1^2f_3+f_1f_2^2)/H^9-(3/16)f_1^3f_2/H^15
+    +(3/128)f_1^5/H^21+(4/3)b_2H^2f_3
+    +(4/9)b_2f_1f_2/H^4-(4/81)b_2f_1^3/H^10
+    +(7/6)b_4Hf_1.                                     (5.16)
+```
+
+Write `s=z+3a`, `f_2=(U^2+z^3s^2V)/4`, with `deg U<=7` and `deg V<=10`.
+The exact old-parameter compatibility system is the eight rows
+
+```text
+[z^j] rem_z(N_5,M_5)=0,             j=0,...,7,         (5.17)
+M_5=z^6s^2,
+N_5=243UV^2-3888z^3sVf_3+640b_2z^4sU^3.
+```
+
+Here Euclidean division is in `Q(a)[z]`; `M_5` is monic, so it introduces no
+additional inversion.  The coefficient order is
+`U=(v0,...,v7)`, `V=(w0,...,w10)`,
+`f_3^new=(f3_0,...,f3_14)`, followed by `b_2`.  The full eight expanded rows
+are in `local_band_audit.json`.  For orientation the first three are
+
+```text
+243*v0*w0^2,
+486*v0*w0*w1+243*v1*w0^2,
+486*v0*w0*w2+243*v0*w1^2+486*v1*w0*w1+243*v2*w0^2.
+```
+
+If (5.17) holds, the apparent degrees 22 through 25 of
+`q_5-q5_tail` cancel identically.  The remaining operator has rank 22 and a
+13-dimensional new kernel before the eight nonlinear old-parameter
+conditions.  They are certainly consistent: set `b_2=0` and
+`V=z^3(z+3a)W`, `deg W<=6`.  Then
+
+```text
+N_5=M_5*(243UW^2-3888Wf_3)
+```
+
+identically.  On this affine locus the old free parameters are `U` (8), `W`
+(7), `f_3^new` (15), `f_4^new` (14), and `b_4` (1); adding the 13 new band-5
+directions gives dimension 58 over `Q(a)`, or 59 including `a`.  This is a
+lower bound for a displayed subfamily, not the full band-5 Krull dimension.
+The eight-row component decomposition remains unsolved, so band 4 is the
+deepest band with a complete dimension count and band 5 is the exact pending
+system.
+
+To continue beyond (5.17), one must also restore the curved `u` chart and the
+canonical `T_2,T_3` coefficient relations.  Continuing only the zero-jet
+slice cannot decide the full branch even if it later becomes empty.
+
+## 6. Xu's `delta=5/2` split
+
+Xu's leading data at `delta=5/2` are
+
+```text
+f(sigma)       = p(pi)^6  t^-3   + ...,
+g(sigma)       = p(pi)^9  t^-9/2 + ...,
+T2(sigma)      = p(pi)^5  t^-5/2 + ...,
+(T3)_f(sigma)  = p(pi)^22 t^-11  + ...,
+T3(sigma)      = q(pi)    t^-5   + ...,
+deg p=3,       deg q=40.
+```
+
+Put `x=s^2`, `y=pi/s`.  Then
+
+```text
+Omega(P)(s^2,pi/s)
+ =P(s^-2,a_0+a_1s^2+a_2s^4+pi*s^5).
+```
+
+Integer `x` exponents force `p^6` to be even in `s`.  For monic
+`p=z^3+A z^2+Bz+C`, the nine odd coefficient rows have triangular leading
+pivots
+
+```text
+[z^17]p^6=6A,
+[z^15]p^6 |_(A=0)=6C.
+```
+
+Hence
+
+```text
+p=z(z^2-rho),        rho != 0,        disc(p)=4rho^3.  (6.1)
+```
+
+The parity saturation is explicit.  In `Q[U,A,C,B]` with lex order, add
+`UB-1`.  The wrapped reduced basis is `{UB-1,A,C}`; the wrapper-only and raw
+parity ideals are nonunit, while adjoining `B` gives `[1]`.  The point
+`A=C=0,B=-1,U=-1` is a positive control.  Then set `B=-rho`.
+
+This separates the levels correctly: at radius two the strict-below common
+face is still `z^3`; at radius `5/2` the at-level polynomial is (6.1).  The
+three roots describe a `9+9+9` split of cover roots.  The two roots
+`+sqrt(rho)` and `-sqrt(rho)` are exchanged by denominator-two conjugacy and
+are not thereby proved to be two physical places.
+
+Xu's factorization `q=p^10 q_1`, `deg q_1=10`, reduces
+`p q'-10p'q=kappa*p^14` exactly to
+
+```text
+q_1'=kappa*p^3.
+```
+
+In the monic `T_3` gauge `kappa=10`, and direct integration gives
+
+```text
+q_1=z^10-(15/4)rho*z^8+5rho^2*z^6-(5/2)rho^3*z^4+b_0. (6.2)
+```
+
+Xu's displayed `kappa=-2` is a scalar-equivalent normalization.  In the exact
+ring
+
+```text
+Q[T,b1,...,b9,kappa,b0,rho], lex,  T*rho*kappa-1=0,
+```
+
+there are 12 unknowns excluding the wrapper and ten effective coefficient
+rows.  The reduced component is
+
+```text
+b1,b2,b3, 2b4+5rho^3, b5, b6-5rho^2, b7,
+4b8+15rho, b9, kappa-10.
+```
+
+It has dimension two, with parameters `(rho,b_0)`.  The wrapped ideal is
+nonunit; adjoining `rho` or `kappa` gives `[1]`, and
+`rho=b_0=1,kappa=10,T=1/10` is a positive witness.
+Moreover,
+
+```text
+Res_z(p,q_1)=b_0(4b_0-rho^5)^2/16.
+```
+
+Thus the same witness lies on the optional coprime open; coprimality is not
+needed merely for face survival.
+
+For `u=xy^2`, define
+
+```text
+Hhat=y(u-rho),
+F*=Hhat^6, G*=Hhat^9, T2*=Hhat^5,
+R*=Hhat^10*(u^5-(15/4)rho*u^4+5rho^2*u^3
+             -(5/2)rho^3*u^2+b_0).
+```
+
+Direct differentiation gives
+
+```text
+J(F*,G*)=0,                 J(R*,G*)=45*x*Hhat^22.
+```
+
+All faces pass the inverse-`Omega` old-degree test termwise; maximum degrees
+are `11,66,99,55,145` for `Hhat,F*,G*,T2*,R*`.  The verdict is exactly
+
+```text
+SURVIVES[DELTA-5/2-LEADING-FACE].
+```
+
+It is not a full lift and does not contradict the fixed-radius branch-C
+exclusion.
+
+## 7. Controls
+
+### 7.1 Branch A predecessor
+
+The charged predecessor uses
+
+```text
+h=y^8(y-x)+sum_(j=0)^8 h_0_j y^j,
+A=(h-h|_(y=0))/y,
+beta=bp*A+bq*y+br*x+bs,
+alpha=quotient_y(beta^2,h),
+f=h^2+2beta,
+g=h^3+3beta*h+(3/2)alpha.
+```
+
+In `Q[h_0_8,...,h_0_0,bp,bq,br,bs,c,T]`, the 29 `h`-adic/Jacobian rows have
+14 unknowns excluding `T`.  The first generator is `-c`; after adding
+`Tc-1`,
+
+```text
+1=-(Tc-1)-T(-c).                                         (7.1)
+```
+
+The unsaturated ideal is nonunit.  Exact `Q` and primes
+`32003,32009,32027` all return `[1]`, with declared-ring and wrapper controls.
+This replays `[1]` for `SATURATED-EMPTY[CONTROL-ANSATZ]`; it does not construct
+the missing bridge to Moh's unprinted ten-variable branch-A system.
+
+### 7.2 Branch C
+
+For squarefree `H=z(z-a)(z-b)` with `ab(a-b)k != 0`, the fixed-radius ODE
+forces `R=H^13(z+ell)` and then
+
+```text
+H'(z+ell)+2H-kH=0.
+```
+
+Writing its four coefficient rows as
+
+```text
+f1=5-k,
+f2=(k-4)(a+b)+3ell,
+f3=(3-k)ab-2(a+b)ell,
+f4=ab*ell,
+f5=T*ab(a-b)k-1,
+```
+
+put `s=a+b,p=ab,d=a-b` and
+
+```text
+m1=Tdk(p/2-ell*s), m2=-Tdk*ell, m3=-Tdk/2,
+m4=3T^2d^2k^2ell, m5=-3Tdk*ell^2-1.
+```
+
+Direct expansion verifies
+
+```text
+1=m1f1+m2f2+m3f3+m4f4+m5f5.                            (7.2)
+```
+
+The unsaturated system has a witness (`a=b=ell=0,k=5`), while the wrapped
+system is `[1]` over `Q` and the same three primes.  Thus branch C is
+`SATURATED-EMPTY[FIXED-RADIUS-TWO]`, with no claim about a different radius.
+
+### 7.3 Moh `(16,12)` Appendix-II calibration
+
+Moh p.208 prints the source-shaped `h,A,B,alpha_i,beta_i` ansatz.  Its 77
+Jacobian coefficient equations have 18 unknowns including `c` (plus wrapper
+`T`); the exact rational wrapped ideal is `[1]`, while the raw origin control
+is nonunit.
+
+The independent order-spine replay begins with 23 rows in 18 chart unknowns.
+By descending `h` band it has row counts
+
+```text
+h^5:1, h^4:2, h^3:2, h^2:5, h^1:6, h^0:7.
+```
+
+Seven `Q*` pivots, with coefficients
+
+```text
+3,6,3,6,3,-12,-9/4,
+```
+
+leave 15 rows in 11 unknowns.  The resolved ring map was checked on all 23
+original generators.  The remaining positive grading permits the torus slice
+`x=1`; over `Q[y]/(H)` with
+
+```text
+H=54y^2-36y+5,
+```
+
+four affine pivots leave the coefficient-field unit
+
+```text
+u=20y-10/3,       v=27/10-27y/5,
+u*v-1=-2H,        hence 1=u*v+2H.                       (7.3)
+```
+
+This is the required positive calibration:
+`SATURATED-EMPTY[ORDER-CHART-CONTROL]`.  It demonstrates that the lifting
+machinery can terminate at the known Appendix-II contradiction without
+pretending the replay variables are Moh's unprinted eta variables.
+
+## 8. Audit and reproduction
+
